<title>BRAZIL: No Brazilian soybean/meal tax proposal-Finance Min.</title>
<headline>No Brazilian soybean/meal tax proposal-Finance Min.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Finance Ministry says it does not know of any proposal to put a tax on soybean or soymeal exports as rumored in the Chicago futures market, said a spokesman for the ministry's price monitoring department.</p>
<p>&quot;The Finance Ministry is not formulating any proposal to put a tax on soybean or soymeal exports and knows of no proposal to do so,&quot; the spokesman said.  </p>
<p>Several months ago crushers had lobbied for a tax on soybeans arguing that otherwise domestic supply would be jeopardised but the ministry had at that point decided that this was not the case and this position had not changed, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>Moreover there had been no fresh requests to reconsider the tax issue, he added.</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
